  "pass_rule": "honest: the four architectures make the same decisions (commands and slots), every command runs and every substation gets a fresh decision in every slot; one site lost: A and B fail over, C and D decide exactly as without the loss, at most one slot missed; two sites lost at 45 %: B's table trips no UFLS, C and D decide exactly as without the loss and trip no UFLS after the strike; two sites lost at 25 %: B's table trips UFLS again in every run, C and D never after the strike; no collapse anywhere. Sweep (two sites lost, supply after the strike 20 to 50 %): C and D never trip UFLS after the strike or collapse; B's table trips UFLS again in every run below its 40 % plan",
  "all_passed": true,
  "known_issues": [
    "UFLS sheds whole stages until the load fits G(t), with no limit on the imbalance it can arrest, so B's table overloads end in UFLS, not in a collapse, unless the critical feeders alone exceed G(t) (UFLS exempts them: sweep point 20 %); with that limit (real UFLS schemes are designed for imbalances up to about 25 to 50 %) the same overloads could black the island out",
    "the policy pays for no UFLS and a fair rotation in energy: it plans with a 5 % reserve, whole feeders and the cold-load pickup of every feeder it restores, so after the strike at 50 % the customer demand it serves is about 70 % of G(t) (about 83 % with the pickup). Holding state (A without centres) and B's table plus UFLS pack the load up to G(t) and rotate less, so they can serve more energy (A from 35 %, B from 25 to 35 %); the price is UFLS events decided by relay stage instead of by the rules, and for A the same feeders dark all day (fairness 0.62 to 0.74)",
    "B's substations re-close feeders that UFLS tripped when the table says so; a scheme that locks tripped feeders out would trip less and serve less",
    "after losing both centres A holds its state (question 26): its feeders stay as they were, UFLS acts when the load grows and nothing rotates; after a collapse (sweep point 20 %) nothing re-closes, so the island is live again after the blackstart but every feeder stays open: dark_h counts only the hour before the blackstart, critical_served_share shows the rest",
    "the loads, the island and the supply profile are illustrative assumptions (loads.py, config.py), not measured data"
  ]
